  "prefLabel": "Env-A 4103.31 Hair shine",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 4103.31 “Hair shine” means any product designed for the primary purpose of creating a shine when applied to the hair, including but not limited to dual-use products designed primarily to impart a sheen to the hair. The term does not include hair spray, hair mousse, hair styling gel, hair styling product, or products whose primary purpose is to condition or hold the hair.\n\nSource. #10527, eff 2-26-14; ss by #13969, eff 5-21-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a4100.html"
